From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: do not link a switch to its own conduit device

When the DSA switch and its conduit are the same device, as on SoCs where
the network engine is both, device_link_add() refuses to make the device
a consumer of itself and the core reports an error for every probe. There
is nothing to order in that case, so skip the link.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/net/dsa/conduit.c b/net/dsa/conduit.c
--- a/net/dsa/conduit.c
+++ b/net/dsa/conduit.c
@@ -425,8 +425,10 @@
 
 	mtu = ETH_DATA_LEN + dsa_tag_protocol_overhead(tag_ops);
 
-	/* The DSA conduit must use SET_NETDEV_DEV for this to work. */
-	if (!netif_is_lag_master(dev)) {
+	/* The DSA conduit must use SET_NETDEV_DEV for this to work. A switch
+	 * that is its own conduit's parent has nothing to be ordered against.
+	 */
+	if (!netif_is_lag_master(dev) && ds->dev != dev->dev.parent) {
 		consumer_link = device_link_add(ds->dev, dev->dev.parent,
 						DL_FLAG_AUTOREMOVE_CONSUMER);
 		if (!consumer_link)
